-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"8b4bbb94648e325119fbf73708dad03ff0adb6054089c9a4b2f9f70eddc1b641","event_uuid":"d6c7240c-357e-4fd8-b9d9-7a82fef0b79c","position":{"commit_sha":"fb3d1943bce8495a20dc1f7ed9eb66864558f9a2","position":"1787095421037421001-d6c7240c-357e-4fd8-b9d9-7a82fef0b79c"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"ae049809c98e5c528a8eeef0a5d8a436f549bdde79cef971ac1ece9e0de7af6f","event_uuid":"d044a273-bca4-45f4-9b94-b50257df0786","position":{"commit_sha":"8155816ab0b342cdac762fa6700696f8cf7ddf0e","position":"1787096024545958001-d044a273-bca4-45f4-9b94-b50257df0786"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"PLAN. Epic 5e64-d9cd-2dd4-4036 (citric-moudly-vipersquid) RP-02: 13 tickets, depth 3 = 3 stories x 3 tasks. Dependency/stack order: S1 mica-governing-buck [T1 vivacious-widish-indianabat -> T2 evadable-curious-mastodon -> T3 patterned-fossillike-betafish] -> S2 brainy-cooked-hog [T1 dermatoid-brassy-junco -> T2 sportive-statued-goose -> T3 morose-selfaware-unicorn] -> S3 convergent-pinelike-lunamoth [T1 polarized-servile-jenny -> T2 flamboyant-possessive-blackbuck -> T3 likeminded-wearproof-barracuda]. All 9 tasks are code leaves; S1T3 and S3T3 also carry ADR 0099 doc work. Cross-root precondition for S3T3 VERIFIED SATISFIED: RP-04 S3 talismanic-profitable-isopod (6e3b-3d1a-0ff7-44b6) is closed, so its landed apply_handlers.py is the rebase base. WORKTREE /Users/joeoakhart/impl-rp02-binding-store branch impl-rp02-binding-store at origin/main cc49700bf6; venv provisioned, commit-msg Change-Id hook verified. LANDING METHOD (per AGENTS.md/CONTRIBUTING.md, project docs win): Gerrit stacked changes via git push gerrit HEAD:refs/for/main; every commit carries rebar-ticket trailer + DCO sign-off; each change needs LLM-Review +1 AND Verified +1; land by submitting the top of the stack. Ticket events auto-push to origin. ATTESTATIONS: epic, S1, S1T1 certified (currency_basis=file_impact, unaffected by the 25 commits since the 034e1720 certification base); the other 10 are unsigned and will earn review-plan in dependency order as prerequisites close, per the enforced not-yet-claimable fast-fail.","timestamp":1787094675982892001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"S1 T1 vivacious-widish-indianabat (2c81) CLAIMED (epic + S1 mica-governing-buck claimed first; all three were already certified). PHASE 4a CENSUS: T1 is a deliberately pre-cutover internal unit (file_impact is binding_repository.py + its test only, and the ticket's Out-of-scope names facade delegation). Surface slots: CLI = out of scope (internal module, unreachable until T2 cutover); MCP/API tool = out of scope (same); library facade public import path = out of scope BY TICKET DESIGN, T2 evadable-curious-mastodon proves BindingStore facade parity; automated callers (reconciler) = out of scope, reached only after T2; dual-direction read-vs-write = IN SCOPE and proven (load and save both characterized for live, retired, and rotation files). Contention triggers: EXEMPT - T1 adds no lock composition, no retry/backoff, and no cache; it characterizes an existing single save seam. PHASE 4b RED EVIDENCE: authored 27 direct-repository tests in tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/state/test_binding_repository.py; all 27 collect and fail with NotImplementedError against a signature-only scaffold, i.e. genuine absence of behavior rather than an import error (a bare-missing-module ImportError was rejected as invalid RED and replaced with the scaffold). Existing-coverage inventory first (test-design section 1): rotation-failure and two-save convergence are ALREADY fully covered for BindingStore in state/test_get_rotation_heldout.py, so the new tests prove those contracts through the NEW owner rather than duplicating; rows with no prior coverage anywhere were no-eager-write-on-construction, retired-file write failure, retire-time live-replace failure, and alert-persistence failure. PHASE 4c HOLD-OUT: 15 fault/corruption tests physically moved OUT of the worktree to /tmp/rp02-heldout/T1_FULL_test_binding_repository.py; only the 12 happy-path tests remain in tree for the implementer.","timestamp":1787095421037421001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"COORDINATOR STATE CHECK absorbed; four adjustments recorded. (1) RP-04 S3 talismanic-profitable-isopod CLOSED - independently verified - so S3 runs in natural T1->T2->T3 order and S3 T3 is NOT deferred. (2) RP-04 did not remove the mutation-through-query pattern: it is still live at apply_handlers.py:261 inside _observe_rich_reemit, and RP-04 added a docstring at ~250-256 asserting that binding_store.py 'sits at the module-size cap and cannot carry a narrower accessor... If that file is ever split along a call-graph seam, give it a single-entry accessor and use it here.' Verified verbatim in the worktree. RP-02 S2 T3 adds exactly that accessor, so the docstring becomes FALSE when S3 T3 lands; S3 T3 must update it in the SAME change. Per the skill this is a NON-BEHAVIORAL comment-accuracy fix - applied directly, no manufactured change-detector test. (3) Attestations independently confirmed: epic/S1/S1T1 certified; S2, S3 and all remaining tasks UNSIGNED. review-plan will be earned mid-run IN DEPENDENCY ORDER (S2's only after S1 closes, S3's only after S2 closes); no front-loading and no --force. (4) MODULE-SIZE headroom verified against the real gate in .github/workflows/_build-and-test.yml: the cap comparison is awk '$1 > lim', i.e. STRICTLY greater, so 800 passes and 801 fails; a non-blocking near-cap warning band starts at 720. Current: binding_store.py 799 (passes, in the warning band; T2 is what brings it down), run_differs.py 739 -> only 61 lines of headroom, so S3 T2 keeps the classifier in binding_recovery.py and limits the run_differs edit to the invocation; reconcile_helpers.py 758 -> S1 T3 preserves the five-file publication seam there without adding to it; apply_handlers.py 553 fine. Every intermediate stack commit must satisfy the cap, not just the final state - the cap number and lint/format rules are shipped in every implementer brief. Also confirmed none of binding_repository.py / binding_lifecycle.py / binding_recovery.py / docs/adr/0099 existed at branch point, so RP-02 is a clean start.","timestamp":1787096024545958001}],"created_at":1787094646738024001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"943ea9fc-e09b-4ab9-beec-5095c57bf9ab","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"5e64-d9cd-2dd4-4036"}],"description":"","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[["relates_to","5e64-d9cd-2dd4-4036"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":[],"ticket_id":"d95a-aa80-dfe0-4336","ticket_type":"session_log","title":"Implement RP-02 citric-moudly-vipersquid: decompose binding persistence, lifecycle, recovery behind BindingStore","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["ebef6fe2-6c65-4cd3-b094-0e1b1a24a53c","943ea9fc-e09b-4ab9-beec-5095c57bf9ab","9f7dd895-06fe-446e-9f99-2aa5bfc3bf0f","d6c7240c-357e-4fd8-b9d9-7a82fef0b79c","d044a273-bca4-45f4-9b94-b50257df0786"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787096024545958002,"uuid":"d875505b-f958-4703-b624-b6e40e18df90"}